 "help": "usage: wgsextract qc fake-data [-h] [--coverage COVERAGE]\n                               [--build {38,grch38,hg38,hs38,hs38d1,hs38d1v0,hs38dh,GRCh38,hs38DH,37,grch37,hg19,hg37,hs37,hs37d5,GRCh37,chm13,chm13v2,chm13v2.0,t2t,t2tv2,t2tv2.0,t2tv20,T2Tv20,T2Tv2,T2Tv2.0,CHM13,CHM13v2.0}]\n                               [--type TYPE] [--full-size] [--legacy-bam] [--seed SEED]\n\noptions:\n  -h, --help            show this help message and exit\n  --coverage COVERAGE   Coverage depth (e.g. 30.0)\n  --build {38,grch38,hg38,hs38,hs38d1,hs38d1v0,hs38dh,GRCh38,hs38DH,37,grch37,hg19,hg37,hs37,hs37d5,GRCh37,chm13,chm13v2,chm13v2.0,t2t,t2tv2,t2tv2.0,t2tv20,T2Tv20,T2Tv2,T2Tv2.0,CHM13,CHM13v2.0}\n                        Human genome build naming convention.\n  --type TYPE           Comma-separated list of types to generate (vcf, cram, bam, fastq, all).\n                        Default: cram\n  --full-size           Use real human chromosome lengths. The default scaled mode uses shorter\n                        chromosomes.\n  --legacy-bam          Use the older scaled fake BAM generator. Slower and unavailable with\n                        --full-size, but includes randomized placement and indel CIGARs.\n  --seed SEED           Random seed for reproducibility\n\nglobal options:\n  -i/--input, -o/--outdir, --genome, --ref, -t/--threads, -m/--memory, --json, --quiet, --debug,\n  --config and the other global options are accepted before or after the command; 'wgsextract\n  --help' lists them all.\n\nexamples:\n  wgsextract qc fake-data --outdir out/fake --type bam,vcf --seed 1\n\noutputs (in the output directory unless noted):\n  fake.cram, fake.bam, fake.vcf or fake_R1/_R2.fastq.gz, and the fake\n  reference.\n\nneeds:\n  bcftools, bgzip, samtools, tabix; depending on options and inputs, also:\n  sambamba; seconds for small inputs.\n",
